# A token copy of Enduring Curiosity (Three Steps Ahead's {3} mode) has the dies ability, since the token was a creature, but the token ceases to
# exist in the graveyard (CR 111.7), so there is nothing to return (ruling 2024-11-08). Bot2's Lightning Bolt kills the token on turn 4: Bot1 has only
# the original Curiosity, still a creature (the positive control: the original is not touched), and no enchantment came back.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Enduring Curiosity
Three Steps Ahead
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Enduring Curiosity.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Three Steps Ahead.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Create a token)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Enduring Curiosity)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Enduring Curiosity#2.Token = true
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Enduring Curiosity#2)
Bot2.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Island; Mox Sapphire; Mox Pearl; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Enduring Curiosity
Bot1.Battlefield.Enduring Curiosity.Types = Enchantment; Creature
Bot1.Graveyard = Three Steps Ahead
Stack.Count = 0
